3. Sharing and modifications
When distributing the software, keep this license and the copyright notices,
mark modified versions as such, and provide recipients with the corresponding
source code under this license, including your modifications and the build
instructions. Do not present a modified version as the official M:orph.
The name and logo follow section 4 below.

4. Name and logo
The M:orph name (with the subtitle Media Browser), mark and app icons identify
the official project; the code permission does not grant their unrestricted
use. You may use them to discuss, review, link to or teach M:orph, show
screenshots of the official app, and share unchanged official builds free
of charge. You may describe a fork as "based on M:orph" or "a fork of M:orph".
Without written permission, do not use the name, logo or confusingly similar
branding for your own product, package, repository, domain or account, and
do not imply that the author makes, supports, approves or endorses your work.
Publish modified versions with their own name and logo, not merely recolored
or cropped copies of ours. These rules cover the artwork in docs/brand/,
build/icon.*, build/icons/ and the mark drawn by src/BrandMark.tsx.
Official builds are those published on this repository's Releases page.
When sharing an unchanged official build, identify it as a third-party copy
and link to the official download. Sales must also comply with section 2.

